{
  "rationale": "The plant separates perception (obstacle events) from motion commands. The specification binds sensor outcomes to safe, progress-oriented actions: move_forward or random_walk in clear, rotate or move_backward in recovery, and full_rotate only as a last-resort. All uncontrollable events are handled in every state. The design ensures the robot quickly returns to exploration after recovery, avoids oscillation, and never enables unsafe actions in obstacle states.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for perception and motion to reflect the robot's sensing and actuation structure.",
    "Specification automaton encodes safe, progress-maximizing action selection, conservative recovery, and rapid return to exploration after obstacles clear."
